WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:10.500
On October 1st ,1949, Mao Zedong
proclaimed that the Chinese people have

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:15.690
stood up to become a "peace-" and "freedom-loving" nation. 70 years, later has this

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:21.119
dream been realized? A look at China
today clearly shows it has not. Certainly

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:25.650
China is not a freedom-loving nation. Its
mass crackdown on political dissidents

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.570
and oppression of religious minorities
demonstrates its continued

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:34.440
authoritarianism. It is also not a
peace-loving nation. It is building up

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.399
its military to challenge the United
States and coerce US allies in Asia.

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:44.430
However, in the last 40 years, China has
achieved much. China's economic growth

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:48.300
has lifted millions out of poverty and
propelled it into one of the world's

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:53.809
largest economies. China has also made
great strides in technology advancement.

00:00:53.809 --> 00:00:58.199
Unfortunately, what has not accompanied
this growth is greater political freedom.

00:00:58.199 --> 00:01:01.949
I hope that in the next 70 years the
Chinese people

00:01:01.949 --> 00:01:07.470
will eventually enjoy the promises made
to them in 1949. Do you think the Chinese

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:11.250
Do you think the Chinese people will really stand up to the Chinese Communist Party? Let us know in

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:15.479
our poll. Also, let us know what other
topics you'd like our scholars to cover

00:01:15.479 --> 00:01:20.009
in 60 seconds, and be sure to like and
subscribe for more research and videos

00:01:20.009 --> 00:01:23.780
from AEI.

